adesantvicent","ibiza"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Cala de Sant Vicent is a beach resort village on the Spanish island of Ibiza. The resort is in the municipality of Sant Joan de Labritja. The resort is reached along the designated roads EI-321 east from Sant Joan de Labritja, and on the EI-200 north from Santa Eulària des Riu.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Cala de Sant Vicent","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Cala_de_San_Vicent%2C_Ibiza.JPG/1280px-Cala_de_San_Vicent%2C_Ibiza.JPG","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Cala_de_San_Vicent%2C_Ibiza.JPG/500px-Cala_de_San_Vicent%2C_Ibiza.JPG","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"BuzzWoof","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cala_de_San_Vicent,_Ibiza.JPG"}},{"id":"ibiza_sa_caleta_battery","areaId":"ibiza","name":"Sa Caleta Battery","category":"monument","tags":["history","views"],"location":{"lat":38.8672,"lng":1.33416},"visitMinutes":90,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"ibiza_sa_caleta_battery","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":15,"commonsNearby":12,"wikiPageviews":48,"wikidataSitelinks":2,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-18"},"hashtags":["sacaletabattery","ibiza"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"The Sa Caleta Coastal Battery is a coastal defence consisting of a set three open gun emplacements built between 1936 and 1937, by the Nationalist during the Spanish Civil war to protect the approaches to Ibiza Airport on the Spanish Island of Ibiza, Spain.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Sa Caleta Coastal Battery","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/The_Sa_Caleta_Coastal_Battery%2C_Ibiza_25_June_2013_%282%29.JPG/1280px-The_Sa_Caleta_Coastal_Battery%2C_Ibiza_25_June_2013_%282%29.JPG","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/The_Sa_Caleta_Coastal_Battery%2C_Ibiza_25_June_2013_%282%29.JPG/500px-The_Sa_Caleta_Coastal_Battery%2C_Ibiza_2